    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (78.91) and **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) emerge as our premier offensive engines. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is the clear anchor, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Singer and an elite BvP history that adds significant weight to his output. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** earns a massive boost from a high-upside matchup against Houser; his dynamic platoon edge and the favorable park factor elevate him well above his base projection, making him a must-start despite his lower spot in the order. **Taylor Ward** (70.38) also warrants attention, as his lead-off role combined with a platoon advantage against Lovelady creates a high-floor profile essential for our daily efficiency targets.\n\nThe decision to keep **Bryson Stott** (45.62) on the bench was the most difficult pivot of the morning. While **Bryson Stott** maintains a strong platoon advantage against Skenes, the matchup against such an elite arm effectively neutralized his base projection, pushing his efficiency below the threshold established by our starting middle infielders, **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Luis Arraez**. Elsewhere, **Daulton Varsho** (61.15) remains a strong play despite the \"Wind In\" warning at his venue; his capacity for production against Flaherty is enough to overcome the atmospheric risk, provided he avoids deep-fly outs at the track. We are monitoring **Jonathan Aranda**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Matt Chapman** to ensure they maintain their projected order slots, as any mid-day lineup shuffle could further compress their marginal scores against their respective opponents.",
